          "gate": "traceability",
          "severity": "minor",
          "source": "reviewer",
          "detail": "D1 [calculations K16, K17, K19; CL15; CL12] Draft-3 adds N+1 node counts (35 nodes at 85%, 37 at 80%, 33 as the memory floor). These counts appear only in the purpose text of K16, K17 and K19. The claimedResult of each calculation is still the steady-state value (33.88, 32, 36). The rounding step, n = ceil(steady-state) + 1, has no calculation entry of its own. A checker that recomputes the K expressions therefore cannot confirm the counts that drive the headline 3-5 node / 420.48-700.80 USD figure. The derivation is correct: (n-1) >= 33.88 gives 35, (n-1) >= 36 gives 37, and (n-1) >= 32 gives 33. K21 checks the 35-node case at 84.71%. There is no matching check for 37 nodes at 80% or 33 nodes at 85% memory, although both work out to exactly the ceiling (2880/36 = 80%, 2720/32 = 85%)."
        }
      ]
    }
